      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(google): add typed Gemini CLI auth boundary",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe bundled Google/Gemini CLI auth boundary needs to support two real cases without leaking raw auth-profile objects across the CLI backend boundary:\n\n- `google` API-backed profiles use API-key credentials.\n- `google-gemini-cli` direct Gemini CLI profiles use OAuth credentials staged into an isolated Gemini CLI auth home.\n\nThis PR keeps the public CLI backend auth-forwarding contract generic, preserves shipped Gemini CLI API-key staging, and makes provider-owned hooks fail closed when they decline forwarding.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added a public provider hook, `resolveCliBackendAuthCredential`, for provider-owned CLI backend credential resolution.\n- Added generic fallback forwarding for standard auth-profile credentials only when the selected provider has no provider-owned hook.\n- Made hook absence distinct from hook decline: a registered hook returning `null` or `undefined` blocks forwarding instead of falling through to generic fallback.\n- Registered the Gemini CLI OAuth resolver on the bundled `google-gemini-cli` provider.\n- Preserved Google API-key fallback forwarding for `google` API-key profiles and Gemini CLI `GEMINI_API_KEY` staging.\n- Preserved backend allowlist checks before and after credential resolution.\n- Fixed CLI runner cleanup gaps on mid-prepare failures.\n- Made bundled MCP fail closed when loopback startup fails instead of writing a partial config.\n- Updated Plugin SDK exports/API baseline and CLI backend plugin docs.\n- Replaced the proof script so it installs the real Google provider/backend registry, verifies the registered provider hook through runtime lookup, runs `prepareCliRunContext`, and executes the staged Gemini CLI auth-home writes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated locally at PR head `6281856ae1`.\n\n```text\npnpm test src/agents/auth-profiles/google.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.test.ts extensions/google/setup-api.test.ts extensions/google/index.test.ts extensions/google/index-harness-registration.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/provider-catalog-shared.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 3 Vitest shards passed, 110 tests passed.\n\n```text\npnpm tsx scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts\n```\n\nResult: passed. The proof output included:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"registeredGeminiCliProviderHook\": true,\n  \"googleApiKeyProviderUsesGenericFallback\": true,\n  \"cliRunnerForwardedOauthViaRegisteredProviderHook\": true,\n  \"cliRunnerForwardedApiKeyViaGenericFallback\": true,\n  \"apiKeyProfileSelectedForGoogle\": true,\n  \"oauthProfileSelectedForGeminiCli\": true,\n  \"geminiCliUsesIsolatedAuthHome\": true,\n  \"inheritedGoogleAuthEnvCleared\": true,\n  \"apiKeyNotWrittenIntoGeminiCliOAuthFiles\": true,\n  \"apiKeyProfileStagesGeminiApiKey\": true,\n  \"apiKeyProfileDoesNotLeaveOauthFiles\": true,\n  \"oauthTokenValuesRedactedFromProofOutput\": true,\n  \"profileIdHashUsedInHome\": true,\n  \"rawProfileIdAbsentFromHome\": true,\n  \"selectedCredentialKinds\": {\n    \"google-gemini-cli\": \"oauth\",\n    \"google\": \"api_key\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```text\npnpm plugin-sdk:api:check\n```\n\nResult: `OK docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256`.\n\n```text\ngit diff --check\npnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/google/gemini-cli-provider.ts scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.test.ts src/plugins/provider-hook-runtime.ts src/plugins/provider-runtime.ts src/plugins/provider-runtime.runtime.ts src/plugins/types.ts\n```\n\nResult: both passed.\n\n## What Was Not Tested\n\nI did not perform a live Gemini CLI OAuth login against a real Google account. The deterministic proof exercises the registered provider hook, CLI runner preparation, forwarding allowlists, isolated auth-home staging, env clearing, API-key staging, redaction, SDK baseline, and focused regression coverage in-process.\n\nI did not run the full repository test suite; the focused suite covers the changed auth boundary, Gemini staging, CLI preparation, SDK export, provider registration, and proof behavior.\n\n## Tests\n\nAI-assisted: yes.",
